{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-abeaa15d-00e1-40b2-8ce2-d6665ab1a6f9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-be9b02ccd8615c5a","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic_case-021-real-pqc-base-image-compliance_0_yhs98llf/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E001.md","content":"# Confirm PQC base image variant availability and RHEL 9.8 rebase date with AIPCC\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves the strategy's two dependency unknowns with the AIPCC team, both tracked under the RHOAIENG-7195 spike:\n\n1. Whether PQC variants of the `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/python-312-minimal`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22` base images will be available for RHOAI 3.6, and their committed delivery dates. These variants are currently unconfirmed; roughly eleven RHOAI images (training variants, lmes-job, feature-server, dashboard) build on them and have no confirmed PQC target base.\n2. The committed date of the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258), which gates adoption of the `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` base image by the ~34 RHOAI images currently built on `rhel9-6-els/rhel:9.6-*` bases.\n\nBoth questions are attributed to the same AIPCC coordination effort and produce one deliverable, so they are combined into a single investigation. The answers determine whether the affected image families proceed with base image switches or fall back to OCP exception filings, and they populate the target-base entries of the PQC readiness matrix.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Engage with the AIPCC team (via the RHOAIENG-7195 spike and AIPCC-7258) to obtain, per base image (python-311, python-312, python-312-minimal, nodejs-22): a confirmed availability status and a committed delivery date.\n- Obtain the committed date for the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase that gates `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` adoption.\n- Verify claimed-available images in registry.redhat.io (e.g., that published PQC variants report `DEFAULT:PQ` under `update-crypto-policies --show`), consistent with the August 2026 confirmation for `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc` and `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`.\n- Record the outcome per image family: switch-by-deadline confirmed, or not-available-in-time (triggering OCP exception filings by the affected component teams).\n- Escalate per the strategy's risk mitigation if no committed date is obtained by early September.\n- Communicate outcomes to the component teams whose images depend on each answer, and to the PQC readiness matrix.\n\nOut of scope: building or delivering the base image variants themselves (AIPCC's deliverable, tracked in their own pipeline); filing OCP exceptions (each component team files its own); Go ML-KEM, TLSAdherence, and TLS-scanner CI (owned by RHAISTRAT-7816).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Each of `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/python-312-minimal`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22` has a recorded availability status and committed delivery date, sourced from the AIPCC team.\n- The AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258) has a recorded committed date, with an explicit statement of whether it lands before the September 15, 2026 deadline.\n- Any image verified as available in registry.redhat.io is checked to report `DEFAULT:PQ` crypto policy, with the check command and output recorded.\n- A per-family go/no-go determination is published: which image families can complete the PQC base switch for RHOAI 3.6 and which must fall back to OCP exception filings.\n- If any committed date is missing as of early September, an escalation is raised per the strategy's risk mitigation (escalate if no committed date by early September).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image for RHOAI 3.6 / OCP 5.0** — this investigation unblocks (or redirects to exceptions) the python/nodejs-based and rhel9-ELS-based image families, which together account for ~45 of the payload's images.\n- Supports the Dependencies table entries: PQC variants of python-311/312/nodejs (unconfirmed) and AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (gates RHEL9-ELS image adoption).\n\n## Risks and Assumptions Carried Forward\n\n- Risk: PQC variants of python-311/312/nodejs not available in time — teams using those bases may need OCP exceptions (mitigated by this investigation and early-September escalation).\n- Risk: AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase slips — teams using rhel9-6-els may need exceptions.\n- Assumption: `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc` and `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` are available and activate DEFAULT:PQ policy (confirmed August 2026, OCPSTRAT-7413) — not re-litigated here.\n"}}],"model":"zai-org/GLM-5.3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":104452,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-abfbe2b1297d6a9a","agent_id":"aad452a5752ce3ae8","session_id":"ffc190d1-a457-4608-ad90-0fad47057ac1","uuid":"7efc05f4-c835-46b0-910e-e0afae362954","timestamp":"2026-10-09T14:20:40.129Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
