e (PQC enablement is runtime only).\n- Note for Go components: ML-KEM arrives via native Go crypto regardless of base; the switch is for platform consistency (confirmed assumption, July 2026). The switch must not change HA characteristics (no replica or availability changes).\n- Includes images of components whose TLS stack is not OpenSSL-backed (e.g., the Rust guardrails orchestrator, whose TLS remediation is tracked separately): the base switch here delivers platform consistency and system-OpenSSL compliance, while those components' ML-KEM negotiation capability is resolved by their own remediation work or OCP exceptions.\n\nOut of scope: OCP exception filing (each team files its own via OCPEXCEPT); Go ML-KEM, TLSAdherence, TLS-scanner CI (RHAISTRAT-7816); post-OCP-5.0 base image evolution (micro images, Hummingbird/UBI10); FIPS+PQC combined support (incompatible on UBI9).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Every image in the ubi9-minimal family has its final runtime stage rebuilt on `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`, or is covered by a filed and acknowledged OCP exception with a documented remediation plan — zero unaccounted-for images remain in this family.\n- For each switched image, `update-crypto-policies --show` executed inside the container reports `DEFAULT:PQ`, and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` reports ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024, verified by the automated payload CI scan.\n- No Dockerfile/Containerfile builder stage changed in any switched image; only the final runtime stage base reference changed.\n- Build pipelines for all switched images reference `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc` and produce green builds.\n- No replica count, availability, or HA characteristic changed as a result of the switch.\n- Rollback: each base swap is revertible by restoring the prior base image reference in the component repository and rebuilding (documented per tracking ticket).\n- All family tracking tickets are linked to the parent strategy for the aggregated OCP 5.0 compliance view.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image (`ubi9-minimal-pqc`, `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`, or equivalent) for RHOAI 3.6 / OCP 5.0** — delivers the switch for the largest family (~68 images).\n- **[P0] PQC enablement is runtime only — only the final stage of the Dockerfile/Containerfile changes; no builder image change needed** — encoded as a scope constraint and acceptance criterion.\n- Supports strategy AC-1 (per-family pass criteria) and AC-2 (switched-or-exceptioned accounting).\n\n## Assumptions Carried Forward\n\n- Go components get ML-KEM via native Go crypto; the base switch is for platform consistency (confirmed July 2026).\n- PQC hybrid key exchange is negotiated opportunistically — clients without PQC support continue via classic ECDHE (backwards compatibility preserved by the base image's OpenSSL).\n- Strategy-level Licence Validation gate is pending human review; a base image content swap is not expected to change transitive dependency licensing, but the gate must clear before ship.\n"}}],"model":"zai-org/GLM-5.3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":105756,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-abfbe2b1297d6a9a","agent_id":"aad452a5752ce3ae8","session_id":"ffc190d1-a457-4608-ad90-0fad47057ac1","uuid":"dbe143c3-eeef-4ed0-950e-dde94135f2ee","timestamp":"2026-10-09T14:21:00.405Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
