e the migration does not change HA characteristics (no replica or availability changes).\n- If the migration cannot land by September 15: file the OCP exception via OCPEXCEPT documenting the component's TLS stack and the reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM, with this epic rewritten to the remediation plan timeline.\n\nOut of scope: the component's ubi9-minimal base image switch (platform-wide switch campaign); Go ML-KEM, TLSAdherence, TLS-scanner CI (RHAISTRAT-7816); ML-DSA certificates (deferred); FIPS+PQC combined support.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The service negotiates ML-KEM hybrid key exchange on its TLS surfaces after migration, demonstrated by a test connection against the migrated stack.\n- Non-PQC TLS 1.3 clients continue to connect via classic ECDHE (opportunistic hybrid negotiation preserved).\n- Existing optional TLS/mTLS and per-service downstream TLS configuration behavior is preserved — no reduction in TLS capabilities.\n- No replica count, availability, or HA characteristic changed as a result of the migration.\n- Rollback: the TLS stack change is revertible by restoring the prior stack configuration and rebuilding; the fallback path if migration is infeasible by the deadline is a filed and acknowledged OCP exception with a documented remediation plan including the component's TLS stack and reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM.\n- The migration (or the exception filing, if that path is taken) is complete before the September 15, 2026 deadline, and the component's tracking ticket is linked to the parent strategy.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image... for RHOAI 3.6 / OCP 5.0** — delivers this component's route to ML-KEM compliance that the base image switch cannot provide (rustls+ring is not OpenSSL-backed).\n- **[P0] Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception via OCPEXCEPT with a remediation plan** — the exception path is this epic's recorded fallback.\n- Supports the strategy's Security NFR (ML-KEM hybrid key exchange for non-Go components), Backwards compatibility NFR (opportunistic hybrid), and Availability NFR (no HA changes).\n\n## Dependencies and Gating\n\n- Gated by the TLS migration spike (RHOAIENG-7452): the spike's outcome rewrites this epic's approach. If the spike finds no feasible migration path before the deadline, the team files an OCP exception with a remediation plan and this epic is re-scoped to that plan.\n"}}],"model":"zai-org/GLM-5.3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":110307,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-abfbe2b1297d6a9a","agent_id":"aad452a5752ce3ae8","session_id":"ffc190d1-a457-4608-ad90-0fad47057ac1","uuid":"7418db5c-7171-474c-98a8-5a2859506d78","timestamp":"2026-10-09T14:22:05.831Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
