{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-5c10bcc9-8d41-4742-9f05-7133a00a039a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-abbcdd77c1568910","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic_case-021-real-pqc-base-image-compliance_0_yhs98llf/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E008.md","content":"# Remediate trainer data cache TLS stack for ML-KEM hybrid support\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic remediates the trainer data cache's TLS stack to support ML-KEM (FIPS 203) hybrid key exchange — but only if the TLS posture audit (RHOAIENG-7196) determines the component uses a pure-Rust TLS stack that cannot inherit PQC from a base image. If the audit finds an OpenSSL-backed stack, no remediation is needed (the platform-wide base image switch delivers PQC compliance for the component) and this epic is removed.\n\nPer the strategy's Security NFR, Rust components using pure-Rust TLS stacks must support ML-KEM hybrid key exchange after migration. If the remediation cannot land before the September 15, 2026 deadline, the trainer team files an OCP exception via OCPEXCEPT with a remediation plan instead.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement the remediation path recommended by the audit so the trainer data cache negotiates ML-KEM hybrid key exchange on its TLS connections.\n- Preserve opportunistic hybrid negotiation — non-PQC TLS 1.3 clients continue to work via classic ECDHE (backwards compatibility NFR).\n- Validate the remediation does not change HA characteristics (no replica or availability changes).\n- If remediation cannot land by September 15: the trainer team files the OCP exception documenting the component's TLS stack and the reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM, with a remediation plan; this epic is then re-scoped to that plan.\n\nOut of scope: the trainer component's base image switch (platform-wide switch campaign); Go ML-KEM and TLS-scanner CI (RHAISTRAT-7816); ML-DSA certificates (deferred).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The data cache negotiates ML-KEM hybrid key exchange after remediation, demonstrated by a test connection against the migrated stack.\n- Non-PQC TLS 1.3 clients continue to connect via classic ECDHE (opportunistic hybrid negotiation preserved).\n- No replica count, availability, or HA characteristic changed as a result of the remediation.\n- Rollback: the TLS stack change is revertible by restoring the prior stack configuration and rebuilding; the fallback path is the OCP exception filing with a documented remediation plan.\n- The remediation (or the exception filing, if that path is taken) is complete before the September 15, 2026 deadline, and the component's tracking ticket is linked to the parent strategy.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image... for RHOAI 3.6 / OCP 5.0** — delivers this component's route to ML-KEM compliance if the base image switch cannot provide it.\n- **[P0] Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception via OCPEXCEPT with a remediation plan** — the exception path is this epic's recorded fallback.\n- Supports the strategy's Security NFR (ML-KEM hybrid for pure-Rust TLS stacks), Backwards compatibility NFR, and Availability NFR.\n\n## Dependencies and Gating\n\n- Gated by the trainer data cache TLS posture audit (RHOAIENG-7196): if the audit finds an OpenSSL-backed stack, this epic is removed — no remediation is needed. If the audit finds a pure-Rust stack, this epic proceeds on the audit's recommended path.\n"}}],"model":"zai-org/GLM-5.3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":112273,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-abfbe2b1297d6a9a","agent_id":"aad452a5752ce3ae8","session_id":"ffc190d1-a457-4608-ad90-0fad47057ac1","uuid":"57760f0c-007b-44c2-82fa-9025b6f5bff2","timestamp":"2026-10-09T14:22:29.090Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
