{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-8a32fc8c-1735-44af-b84d-51cb7387854f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-93498919df941c24","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic_case-021-real-pqc-base-image-compliance_0_yhs98llf/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E009.md","content":"# PQC readiness matrix and compliance coordination\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the strategy's coordination work: the PQC Readiness Matrix per component (a design doc the strategy marks \"to be created\"), aggregation of component team tracking tickets linked to the parent strategy for OCP 5.0 visibility, enforcement of the OCP exception process for teams that cannot comply by September 15, and the weekly reminder/escalation cadence agreed in the Mara/Devin sync decision.\n\nThis is the primary effort of the strategy as a compliance coordination tracker: aggregating team compliance status via linked tickets and ensuring the exception process is exercised by September 15 so that zero RHOAI component images remain unaccounted for.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Create and maintain the PQC Readiness Matrix per component: current base image, target PQC base (or TBD pending the AIPCC confirmation), TLS stack, switch/exception status, and owning team — sourced from the RHOAI 3.5 CSV relatedImages list, the locally maintained organized image inventory, and component architecture context.\n- Ensure every component team's tracking ticket is linked to the parent strategy (RHAISTRAT-8001), providing the aggregated compliance view for OCP 5.0.\n- Track the exception path: components expected to file OCP exceptions (TrustyAI explainability service — Java/NSS, JDK 29 timeline September 2027; fms-guardrails-orchestrator if its TLS migration cannot land in time; trainer data cache if remediation cannot land in time; any python/nodejs-based component if PQC base variants are not available in time) each have a filed and acknowledged OCPEXCEPT exception with a remediation plan including the component's TLS stack and the reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM.\n- Run the weekly reminder cadence to teams and escalate to leadership per the Mara/Devin sync decision when the September 15 deadline is at risk without an exception filed.\n- Record the FIPS-mode exclusion in the compliance accounting: on FIPS-mode clusters, FIPS policy deactivates PQC for this release — expected behavior, not a compliance failure.\n- Update matrix entries as the AIPCC confirmation resolves python/nodejs target bases and as audits resolve Rust TLS postures.\n\nOut of scope: filing individual teams' OCP exceptions (each team files its own via OCPEXCEPT); executing image switches (family campaigns); Go ML-KEM, TLSAdherence, TLS-scanner CI (RHAISTRAT-7816); ML-DSA certificates (deferred).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The PQC Readiness Matrix exists and covers every RHOAI component image, with per-image current base, target base (or documented TBD), TLS stack, and status.\n- By September 15, 2026: every RHOAI component image is accounted for in the matrix as either (a) rebuilt on a PQC-enabled base image or (b) covered by a filed and acknowledged OCP exception with a documented remediation plan — zero unaccounted-for images remain.\n- All component team tracking tickets are linked to the parent strategy, providing an aggregated compliance view for OCP 5.0.\n- Teams flagged as likely exception filers have been reminded on the weekly cadence, with escalation to leadership raised where the deadline is at risk without a filing.\n- The matrix records the FIPS-mode exclusion (PQC deactivated on FIPS clusters this release — expected, not a compliance failure).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **[P0] Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception via OCPEXCEPT with a remediation plan** — this epic enforces and tracks the exception process to the zero-unaccounted-images outcome (strategy AC-2).\n- Strategy AC-3: all component team tracking tickets linked to the parent strategy for aggregated OCP 5.0 visibility.\n- Supports all P0 HLRs by providing the aggregated compliance view that verifies them.\n\n## Risks and Assumptions Carried Forward\n\n- Risk: teams miss the September 15 deadline without filing exceptions — creates an untracked compliance gap (mitigation: weekly reminders; escalation to leadership per the Mara/Devin sync decision — this epic owns that mitigation).\n- The strategy's acceptance criteria are marked \"Proposed — requires PM/Engineering validation\"; this epic's matrix and accounting provide the evidence base for that validation.\n"}}],"model":"zai-org/GLM-5.3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":113160,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-abfbe2b1297d6a9a","agent_id":"aad452a5752ce3ae8","session_id":"ffc190d1-a457-4608-ad90-0fad47057ac1","uuid":"61dd2878-652a-4241-9d7b-41fa6d652a18","timestamp":"2026-10-09T14:22:43.717Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
