{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-46d9ab2e-3c9c-400a-b23c-e9968865c4fc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a06bd3c8d1af2398","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic_case-021-real-pqc-base-image-compliance_0_yhs98llf/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E010.md","content":"# Automated payload CI scan for PQC crypto policy compliance\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic builds the automated CI scan that measures the strategy's primary acceptance criterion: across the RHOAI 3.6 payload, every switched container reports `DEFAULT:PQ` as its active crypto policy and exposes ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024 via `openssl list -kem-algorithms`. The scan provides the per-image and payload-level compliance verification for the base image switch campaigns.\n\nThis is distinct from the TLS-scanner CI owned by RHAISTRAT-7816 (which tests TLS handshake PQC negotiation): this scan verifies container crypto policy and KEM algorithm availability inside the shipped images.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build a CI job that, for each image in the RHOAI 3.6 payload (enumerated from the RHOAI-Build-Config CSV relatedImages list), executes `update-crypto-policies --show` and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` inside the container and compares against expected values (`DEFAULT:PQ`; ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, ML-KEM-1024 present).\n- Produce a per-image and aggregated compliance report across the payload, consumable by the PQC readiness matrix and compliance coordination tracking.\n- Encode the criterion's documented exclusions: the check applies to OpenSSL-backed components only — components using non-OpenSSL TLS stacks (rustls+ring, Java/NSS) are accounted for by OCP exception filings rather than this scan; on FIPS-mode clusters, FIPS policy deactivates PQC for this release, so `DEFAULT:PQ` non-functionality there is expected and not a compliance failure.\n- Run the scan in CI on the payload build so compliance is measured continuously as images switch.\n\nOut of scope: TLS handshake negotiation testing (TLS-scanner CI, owned by RHAISTRAT-7816); Go ML-KEM testing (RHOAIENG-7334, RHAISTRAT-7816); remediating non-compliant images (the switch campaigns' scope).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The scan executes across the full RHOAI 3.6 payload and produces a per-image compliance result (policy `DEFAULT:PQ`; ML-KEM-512/768/1024 present) plus an aggregated report.\n- OpenSSL-backed images that have completed the base image switch pass the scan; failures identify the image and failing check.\n- Components using non-OpenSSL TLS stacks are excluded from pass/fail and cross-referenced against the exception-tracking accounting instead.\n- FIPS-mode clusters are handled per the documented exclusion: PQC deactivation under FIPS policy for this release is reported as expected behavior, not a compliance failure.\n- The scan runs as part of CI on the payload (not only as a one-off), so the final RHOAI 3.6 payload measurement is reproducible.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image... for RHOAI 3.6 / OCP 5.0** — this epic is the \"measured by automated CI scan across the RHOAI 3.6 payload\" clause of strategy AC-1.\n- **[P0] Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception...** — the scan's exclusion accounting cross-references exception-covered components, supporting the zero-unaccounted-images outcome of AC-2.\n\n## Assumptions Carried Forward\n\n- The image list for RHOAI 3.6 follows the RHOAI-Build-Config CSV relatedImages pattern (153 relatedImages for 3.5) and the locally maintained organized inventory; the scan enumerates from the 3.6 equivalent.\n- X25519MLKEM768 hybrid key exchange is backwards-compatible with non-PQC TLS 1.3 clients (IETF hybrid key exchange draft) — the scan checks algorithm availability, not client compatibility.\n"}}],"model":"zai-org/GLM-5.3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":114260,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-abfbe2b1297d6a9a","agent_id":"aad452a5752ce3ae8","session_id":"ffc190d1-a457-4608-ad90-0fad47057ac1","uuid":"087eaf2e-e3e9-421b-8c98-ab7ec84a77cb","timestamp":"2026-10-09T14:22:57.225Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
