{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-e1f6d57b-9179-420b-a2ab-7d7c319f2506","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9193d8f93c6fbe05","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic_case-021-real-pqc-base-image-compliance_0_yhs98llf/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E011.md","content":"# TLS handshake latency regression threshold and measurement\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic resolves the strategy's Performance NFR, which is flagged NEEDS DOMAIN INPUT (no numeric regression threshold set; owner: PM + Performance team lead; must be resolved before Sprint 2 ends), and delivers the TLS handshake latency regression measurement required before ship (Performance Team Support: Required).\n\nThe epic defines the numeric TLS handshake latency regression threshold, then measures the RHOAI 3.6 PQC-enabled payload against it, producing the pass/fail evidence for the Availability/Performance NFRs of the base image switch.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define, with the PM and Performance team lead, the numeric TLS handshake latency regression threshold for the PQC migration — referencing the Chrome ~10% maximum TLS handshake time regression figure and the Red Hat PQC benchmarking outcome (PSASTRAT-7170) cited by the strategy. Resolution is required before Sprint 2 ends.\n- Define the measurement methodology for TLS handshake latency on the PQC-enabled payload (PQC hybrid handshake vs. classic ECDHE baseline), building on the PSASTRAT-7170 benchmarking outcome.\n- Measure TLS handshake latency regression on the RHOAI 3.6 payload once PQC base image switches have landed (PQC-enabled components negotiating ML-KEM hybrid key exchange vs. baseline).\n- Produce a benchmark report: measured regression vs. threshold, per component class where meaningful, with a pass/fail determination.\n- If the measured regression exceeds the threshold: escalate with a remediation plan (the threshold decision determines whether remediation work is required before ship).\n\nOut of scope: remediating performance regressions (follow-on work if the threshold is exceeded); Go ML-KEM benchmarking owned by RHAISTRAT-7816; micro images / Hummingbird-UBI10 base image evolution (post-OCP-5.0).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A numeric TLS handshake latency regression threshold is documented and approved by the PM and Performance team lead before Sprint 2 ends.\n- The measurement methodology is documented, referencing PSASTRAT-7170 and the Chrome ~10% reference.\n- TLS handshake latency is measured on the PQC-enabled RHOAI 3.6 payload against the classic ECDHE baseline, and the measurement completes before ship.\n- The benchmark report records measured regression vs. threshold with a pass/fail determination; any failure is escalated with a remediation plan.\n- The measurement confirms the base image switch has not changed HA characteristics (no availability regression attributable to the switch).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Supports the strategy's Performance NFR (⚠️ NEEDS DOMAIN INPUT — this epic resolves it), Availability NFR (no HA changes), and the Prerequisites gate \"Performance Team Support: Required — TLS handshake latency regression measurement needed before ship\".\n- Validates the P0 base image switch HLRs: the switch is only shippable if the measured regression is within the approved threshold.\n\n## Open Questions Addressed\n\n- Resolves the strategy's flagged domain-input gap: no numeric regression threshold set for TLS handshake latency (owner PM + Performance team lead, deadline: before Sprint 2 ends).\n"}}],"model":"zai-org/GLM-5.3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":115265,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-abfbe2b1297d6a9a","agent_id":"aad452a5752ce3ae8","session_id":"ffc190d1-a457-4608-ad90-0fad47057ac1","uuid":"39f15b8f-8442-4f9f-9d03-11ec5e75c8bd","timestamp":"2026-10-09T14:23:10.456Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
