{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9fd3e8260c19a9c9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E001\n3\ttitle: Confirm PQC base image variant availability and RHEL 9.8 rebase date with AIPCC\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: AIPCC Productization\n6\tteam: AIPCC team\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Confirm PQC base image variant availability and RHEL 9.8 rebase date with AIPCC\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's two dependency unknowns with the AIPCC team, both tracked under the RHOAIENG-7195 spike:\n30\t\n31\t1. Whether PQC variants of the `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/python-312-minimal`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22` base images will be available for RHOAI 3.6, and their committed delivery dates. These variants are currently unconfirmed; roughly eleven RHOAI images (training variants, lmes-job, feature-server, dashboard) build on them and have no confirmed PQC target base.\n32\t2. The committed date of the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258), which gates adoption of the `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` base image by the ~34 RHOAI images currently built on `rhel9-6-els/rhel:9.6-*` bases.\n33\t\n34\tBoth questions are attributed to the same AIPCC coordination effort and produce one deliverable, so they are combined into a single investigation. The answers determine whether the affected image families proceed with base image switches or fall back to OCP exception filings, and they populate the target-base entries of the PQC readiness matrix.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Engage with the AIPCC team (via the RHOAIENG-7195 spike and AIPCC-7258) to obtain, per base image (python-311, python-312, python-312-minimal, nodejs-22): a confirmed availability status and a committed delivery date.\n39\t- Obtain the committed date for the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase that gates `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` adoption.\n40\t- Verify claimed-available images in registry.redhat.io (e.g., that published PQC variants report `DEFAULT:PQ` under `update-crypto-policies --show`), consistent with the August 2026 confirmation for `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc` and `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`.\n41\t- Record the outcome per image family: switch-by-deadline confirmed, or not-available-in-time (triggering OCP exception filings by the affected component teams).\n42\t- Escalate per the strategy's risk mitigation if no committed date is obtained by early September.\n43\t- Communicate outcomes to the component teams whose images depend on each answer, and to the PQC readiness matrix.\n44\t\n45\tOut of scope: building or delivering the base image variants themselves (AIPCC's deliverable, tracked in their own pipeline); filing OCP exceptions (each component team files its own); Go ML-KEM, TLSAdherence, and TLS-scanner CI (owned by RHAISTRAT-7816).\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- Each of `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/python-312-minimal`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22` has a recorded availability status and committed delivery date, sourced from the AIPCC team.\n50\t- The AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258) has a recorded committed date, with an explicit statement of whether it lands before the September 15, 2026 deadline.\n51\t- Any image verified as available in registry.redhat.io is checked to report `DEFAULT:PQ` crypto policy, with the check command and output recorded.\n52\t- A per-family go/no-go determination is published: which image families can complete the PQC base switch for RHOAI 3.6 and which must fall back to OCP exception filings.\n53\t- If any committed date is missing as of early September, an escalation is raised per the strategy's risk mitigation (escalate if no committed date by early September).\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image for RHOAI 3.6 / OCP 5.0** — this investigation unblocks (or redirects to exceptions) the python/nodejs-based and rhel9-ELS-based image families, which together account for ~45 of the payload's images.\n58\t- Supports the Dependencies table entries: PQC variants of python-311/312/nodejs (unconfirmed) and AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (gates RHEL9-ELS image adoption).\n59\t\n60\t## Risks and Assumptions Carried Forward\n61\t\n62\t- Risk: PQC variants of python-311/312/nodejs not available in time — teams using those bases may need OCP exceptions (mitigated by this investigation and early-September escalation).\n63\t- Risk: AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase slips — teams using rhel9-6-els may need exceptions.\n64\t- Assumption: `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc` and `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` are available and activate DEFAULT:PQ policy (confirmed August 2026, OCPSTRAT-7413) — not re-litigated here.\n65\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfc0faf56a1d8564","agent_id":"aa60bfa32cd2e2564","session_id":"ffc190d1-a457-4608-ad90-0fad47057ac1","uuid":"3d6422cf-1840-4c11-9da8-c36cf2e0c053","timestamp":"2026-10-09T14:37:00.045Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9fd3e8260c19a9c9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
