{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af349ac377aa7063","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E002\n3\ttitle: Switch ubi9-minimal-based runtime images to ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: DevOps/Build\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: -1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Switch ubi9-minimal-based runtime images to ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic coordinates the PQC base image switch campaign for the ~68 RHOAI runtime images currently built on `ubi9/ubi-minimal:latest` — Go operators and most platform components — switching each image's final runtime stage to `registry.redhat.io/ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc` (confirmed available, reports `DEFAULT:PQ`). The target base is confirmed available, so this campaign starts immediately with no dependency on the AIPCC confirmation work.\n34\t\n35\tPer the strategy, each image's owning component team executes the final-stage base swap in its own repository via its tracking ticket linked to the parent strategy; this epic coordinates the campaign: build pipeline updates, per-team tracking, and verification that every image in the family is switched (or covered by an OCP exception).\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Campaign coordination across the component teams owning ubi9-minimal-based images (Go operators and most platform components), using the RHOAI 3.5 CSV relatedImages list (153 relatedImages) and the locally maintained organized image inventory to enumerate the ~68 images in this family.\n40\t- Coordinate build pipeline updates so builds reference `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc` (e.g., RHOAI-Build-Config references and per-repo pipeline configuration).\n41\t- Track each image's switch via the owning team's tracking ticket linked to the parent strategy; chase unlinked tickets weekly per the strategy's mitigation for missed deadlines.\n42\t- Only the final runtime stage of each Dockerfile/Containerfile changes — no builder image change (PQC enablement is runtime only).\n43\t- Note for Go components: ML-KEM arrives via native Go crypto regardless of base; the switch is for platform consistency (confirmed assumption, July 2026). The switch must not change HA characteristics (no replica or availability changes).\n44\t- Includes images of components whose TLS stack is not OpenSSL-backed (e.g., the Rust guardrails orchestrator, whose TLS remediation is tracked separately): the base switch here delivers platform consistency and system-OpenSSL compliance, while those components' ML-KEM negotiation capability is resolved by their own remediation work or OCP exceptions.\n45\t\n46\tOut of scope: OCP exception filing (each team files its own via OCPEXCEPT); Go ML-KEM, TLSAdherence, TLS-scanner CI (RHAISTRAT-7816); post-OCP-5.0 base image evolution (micro images, Hummingbird/UBI10); FIPS+PQC combined support (incompatible on UBI9).\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Every image in the ubi9-minimal family has its final runtime stage rebuilt on `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`, or is covered by a filed and acknowledged OCP exception with a documented remediation plan — zero unaccounted-for images remain in this family.\n51\t- For each switched image, `update-crypto-policies --show` executed inside the container reports `DEFAULT:PQ`, and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` reports ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024, verified by the automated payload CI scan.\n52\t- No Dockerfile/Containerfile builder stage changed in any switched image; only the final runtime stage base reference changed.\n53\t- Build pipelines for all switched images reference `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc` and produce green builds.\n54\t- No replica count, availability, or HA characteristic changed as a result of the switch.\n55\t- Rollback: each base swap is revertible by restoring the prior base image reference in the component repository and rebuilding (documented per tracking ticket).\n56\t- All family tracking tickets are linked to the parent strategy for the aggregated OCP 5.0 compliance view.\n57\t\n58\t## HLR Traceability\n59\t\n60\t- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image (`ubi9-minimal-pqc`, `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`, or equivalent) for RHOAI 3.6 / OCP 5.0** — delivers the switch for the largest family (~68 images).\n61\t- **[P0] PQC enablement is runtime only — only the final stage of the Dockerfile/Containerfile changes; no builder image change needed** — encoded as a scope constraint and acceptance criterion.\n62\t- Supports strategy AC-1 (per-family pass criteria) and AC-2 (switched-or-exceptioned accounting).\n63\t\n64\t## Assumptions Carried Forward\n65\t\n66\t- Go components get ML-KEM via native Go crypto; the base switch is for platform consistency (confirmed July 2026).\n67\t- PQC hybrid key exchange is negotiated opportunistically — clients without PQC support continue via classic ECDHE (backwards compatibility preserved by the base image's OpenSSL).\n68\t- Strategy-level Licence Validation gate is pending human review; a base image content swap is not expected to change transitive dependency licensing, but the gate must clear before ship.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0166ce5350227c5","agent_id":"a9f7d0263db104ceb","session_id":"ffc190d1-a457-4608-ad90-0fad47057ac1","uuid":"0da146c8-cdcb-4b24-9923-cf3a539f0b53","timestamp":"2026-10-09T14:43:21.495Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-af349ac377aa7063","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
