{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad00a71818ef04b0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E003\n3\ttitle: Switch rhel9-ELS-based runtime images to rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: Notebooks Images\n6\tteam: DevOps/Build\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8001-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8001-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase committed date slips past September\n15\t    15, affected teams file OCP exceptions with remediation plans and the campaign\n16\t    scope is rewritten to the images that can still switch.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: -1\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: High\n30\tai_implementability_score: 3\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Switch rhel9-ELS-based runtime images to rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic coordinates the PQC base image switch campaign for the ~34 RHOAI runtime images currently built on `rhel9-6-els/rhel:9.6-*` bases — notebooks, workbenches, training runtimes, and mlserver — switching each image's final runtime stage to `registry.redhat.io/rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` (confirmed available, reports `DEFAULT:PQ`).\n39\t\n40\tAdoption of the rhel9-8-els base is gated on the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258): this campaign starts once the rebase committed date is confirmed to land before the September 15, 2026 deadline. If the rebase date slips past the deadline, the affected component teams file OCP exceptions instead and this campaign's scope is rewritten accordingly.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Campaign coordination across the component teams owning rhel9-6-els-based images (notebook images, workbench images, training runtimes, mlserver), enumerated from the RHOAI 3.5 CSV relatedImages list and the locally maintained organized image inventory.\n45\t- Coordinate build pipeline updates so builds reference `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`.\n46\t- Track each image's switch via the owning team's tracking ticket linked to the parent strategy; weekly chasing per the strategy's deadline mitigation.\n47\t- Only the final runtime stage of each Dockerfile/Containerfile changes — no builder image change (PQC enablement is runtime only).\n48\t- The switch must not change HA characteristics (no replica or availability changes).\n49\t\n50\tOut of scope: OCP exception filing (each team files its own via OCPEXCEPT); post-OCP-5.0 base image evolution; FIPS+PQC combined support; PQC-signed certificates (ML-DSA, deferred).\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- The AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase committed date is confirmed to land before the September 15, 2026 deadline before family-wide execution proceeds; if it slips, affected teams file OCP exceptions and this campaign's scope is rewritten to the images that can still switch.\n55\t- Every image in the rhel9-6-els family has its final runtime stage rebuilt on `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`, or is covered by a filed and acknowledged OCP exception with a documented remediation plan including the component's TLS stack and reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM — zero unaccounted-for images remain in this family.\n56\t- For each switched image, `update-crypto-policies --show` executed inside the container reports `DEFAULT:PQ`, and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` reports ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024, verified by the automated payload CI scan.\n57\t- No Dockerfile/Containerfile builder stage changed in any switched image; only the final runtime stage base reference changed.\n58\t- Build pipelines for all switched images reference `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` and produce green builds.\n59\t- No replica count, availability, or HA characteristic changed as a result of the switch.\n60\t- Rollback: each base swap is revertible by restoring the prior base image reference in the component repository and rebuilding (documented per tracking ticket).\n61\t- All family tracking tickets are linked to the parent strategy for the aggregated OCP 5.0 compliance view.\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image (`ubi9-minimal-pqc`, `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`, or equivalent) for RHOAI 3.6 / OCP 5.0** — delivers the switch for the rhel9-ELS family (~34 images).\n66\t- **[P0] PQC enablement is runtime only — only the final stage changes; no builder image change needed** — encoded as a scope constraint and acceptance criterion.\n67\t- Supports strategy AC-1 (per-family pass criteria) and AC-2 (switched-or-exceptioned accounting).\n68\t\n69\t## Risks Carried Forward\n70\t\n71\t- Risk: AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase slips — gates rhel9-8-els image adoption; teams using rhel9-6-els may need exceptions (mitigation: monitor AIPCC-7258 via the AIPCC confirmation work; escalate if no committed date by early September).\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0166ce5350227c5","agent_id":"a9f7d0263db104ceb","session_id":"ffc190d1-a457-4608-ad90-0fad47057ac1","uuid":"72832b26-ce54-4e70-8097-3a90fbf7bb5a","timestamp":"2026-10-09T14:43:25.794Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad00a71818ef04b0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
