{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-91755320cb6844ba","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E004\n3\ttitle: Switch python/nodejs-based runtime images to PQC base image variants\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: Model Runtimes\n6\tteam: DevOps/Build\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8001-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8001-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: remove\n14\t  fallback_approach: If PQC variants of the python/nodejs base images are not confirmed\n15\t    available for RHOAI 3.6 in time, this epic is removed and the affected component\n16\t    teams file OCP exceptions via OCPEXCEPT by September 15; partial availability\n17\t    reduces scope to the available variants.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: -1\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 1\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Switch python/nodejs-based runtime images to PQC base image variants\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic coordinates the PQC base image switch campaign for the ~11 RHOAI runtime images built on python and nodejs base images: five `ubi9/python-311` images (training variants, lmes-job), four `ubi9/python-312` images (training variants), one `ubi9/python-312-minimal` image (feature-server), and one `ubi9/nodejs-22` image (dashboard).\n40\t\n41\tThe PQC variants of these base images are unconfirmed — the AIPCC spike (RHOAIENG-7195) is tracking availability and committed dates. This campaign exists only if the AIPCC confirmation establishes that the variants are available for RHOAI 3.6 in time; otherwise the affected component teams file OCP exceptions by September 15 and this campaign is removed.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Campaign coordination across the component teams owning python/nodejs-based images (training runtimes, feature-server, dashboard), enumerated from the RHOAI 3.5 CSV relatedImages list and the locally maintained organized image inventory.\n46\t- Coordinate build pipeline updates so builds reference the confirmed PQC variant of each base (python-311, python-312, python-312-minimal, nodejs-22).\n47\t- Track each image's switch via the owning team's tracking ticket linked to the parent strategy; weekly chasing per the strategy's deadline mitigation.\n48\t- Only the final runtime stage of each Dockerfile/Containerfile changes — no builder image change (PQC enablement is runtime only).\n49\t- The switch must not change HA characteristics (no replica or availability changes).\n50\t- For the dashboard's nodejs-22 image: the strategy notes it is largely behind a Go proxy; the campaign follows the same variant-or-exception determination from the AIPCC confirmation.\n51\t\n52\tOut of scope: OCP exception filing (each team files its own via OCPEXCEPT); delivering the PQC base image variants themselves (AIPCC's deliverable); Go ML-KEM and TLS-scanner CI (RHAISTRAT-7816); post-OCP-5.0 base image evolution.\n53\t\n54\t## Acceptance Criteria\n55\t\n56\t- PQC variants of `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/python-312-minimal`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22` are confirmed available in registry.redhat.io before family-wide execution proceeds; if any variant is not available in time, the affected teams file OCP exceptions and this campaign's scope reduces accordingly (potentially to zero images for RHOAI 3.6).\n57\t- Every image in the python/nodejs family has its final runtime stage rebuilt on the confirmed PQC variant of its base, or is covered by a filed and acknowledged OCP exception with a documented remediation plan including the component's TLS stack and reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM — zero unaccounted-for images remain in this family.\n58\t- For each switched image, `update-crypto-policies --show` executed inside the container reports `DEFAULT:PQ`, and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` reports ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024, verified by the automated payload CI scan.\n59\t- No Dockerfile/Containerfile builder stage changed in any switched image; only the final runtime stage base reference changed.\n60\t- Build pipelines for all switched images reference the PQC base variants and produce green builds.\n61\t- No replica count, availability, or HA characteristic changed as a result of the switch.\n62\t- Rollback: each base swap is revertible by restoring the prior base image reference in the component repository and rebuilding (documented per tracking ticket).\n63\t- All family tracking tickets are linked to the parent strategy for the aggregated OCP 5.0 compliance view.\n64\t\n65\t## HLR Traceability\n66\t\n67\t- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image (`ubi9-minimal-pqc`, `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`, or equivalent) for RHOAI 3.6 / OCP 5.0** — delivers the switch for the python/nodejs family (~11 images) once variants are confirmed.\n68\t- **[P0] PQC enablement is runtime only — only the final stage changes; no builder image change needed** — encoded as a scope constraint and acceptance criterion.\n69\t- Supports strategy AC-1 (per-family pass criteria) and AC-2 (switched-or-exceptioned accounting).\n70\t\n71\t## Risks Carried Forward\n72\t\n73\t- Risk: PQC variants of python-311/312/nodejs not available in time — teams using those bases may need OCP exceptions (mitigation: AIPCC spike with committed-date escalation by early September; the confirmation work gates this campaign).\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0166ce5350227c5","agent_id":"a9f7d0263db104ceb","session_id":"ffc190d1-a457-4608-ad90-0fad47057ac1","uuid":"d47f34f4-eae3-491b-b332-f679451ad238","timestamp":"