{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfbec7a371a57a13","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E006\n3\ttitle: Migrate fms-guardrails-orchestrator TLS stack to ML-KEM hybrid key exchange\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: AI Guardrails\n6\tteam: AI Guardrails team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8001-E005\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8001-E005\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: The spike's chosen migration path rewrites this epic's approach;\n15\t    if no migration can land before September 15, the team files an OCP exception\n16\t    via OCPEXCEPT with a remediation plan and the epic is re-scoped to that plan.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: 0\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 2\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Migrate fms-guardrails-orchestrator TLS stack to ML-KEM hybrid key exchange\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic executes the TLS stack migration for fms-guardrails-orchestrator so that the service supports ML-KEM (FIPS 203) hybrid key exchange, per the strategy's Security NFR. The migration approach, effort, and September 15 feasibility are determined by the TLS migration spike (RHOAIENG-7452); this epic implements the recommended path. If the spike determines the migration cannot land before the deadline, the team files an OCP exception via OCPEXCEPT with a remediation plan instead, and this epic's approach is rewritten to the post-deadline remediation.\n39\t\n40\tThe base image switch coordinated in the platform-wide campaign delivers platform consistency for this component's image but does not deliver ML-KEM — rustls+ring does not use system OpenSSL — so this migration is the component's actual route to PQC compliance.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Implement the spike's recommended TLS stack changes so the service negotiates ML-KEM hybrid key exchange (e.g., X25519MLKEM768) on its TLS surfaces: optional inbound TLS/mTLS on the API server and per-service downstream TLS configuration (detector, chunker, generation clients).\n45\t- Preserve existing TLS behavior and configuration surfaces: optional server TLS and client certificate verification, per-service TLS maps in the YAML configuration, header passthrough, and the optional X-Forwarded-Access-Token rewrite.\n46\t- Preserve opportunistic hybrid negotiation — non-PQC TLS 1.3 clients continue to work via classic ECDHE (backwards compatibility NFR).\n47\t- Validate the migration does not change HA characteristics (no replica or availability changes).\n48\t- If the migration cannot land by September 15: file the OCP exception via OCPEXCEPT documenting the component's TLS stack and the reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM, with this epic rewritten to the remediation plan timeline.\n49\t\n50\tOut of scope: the component's ubi9-minimal base image switch (platform-wide switch campaign); Go ML-KEM, TLSAdherence, TLS-scanner CI (RHAISTRAT-7816); ML-DSA certificates (deferred); FIPS+PQC combined support.\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- The service negotiates ML-KEM hybrid key exchange on its TLS surfaces after migration, demonstrated by a test connection against the migrated stack.\n55\t- Non-PQC TLS 1.3 clients continue to connect via classic ECDHE (opportunistic hybrid negotiation preserved).\n56\t- Existing optional TLS/mTLS and per-service downstream TLS configuration behavior is preserved — no reduction in TLS capabilities.\n57\t- No replica count, availability, or HA characteristic changed as a result of the migration.\n58\t- Rollback: the TLS stack change is revertible by restoring the prior stack configuration and rebuilding; the fallback path if migration is infeasible by the deadline is a filed and acknowledged OCP exception with a documented remediation plan including the component's TLS stack and reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM.\n59\t- The migration (or the exception filing, if that path is taken) is complete before the September 15, 2026 deadline, and the component's tracking ticket is linked to the parent strategy.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image... for RHOAI 3.6 / OCP 5.0** — delivers this component's route to ML-KEM compliance that the base image switch cannot provide (rustls+ring is not OpenSSL-backed).\n64\t- **[P0] Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception via OCPEXCEPT with a remediation plan** — the exception path is this epic's recorded fallback.\n65\t- Supports the strategy's Security NFR (ML-KEM hybrid key exchange for non-Go components), Backwards compatibility NFR (opportunistic hybrid), and Availability NFR (no HA changes).\n66\t\n67\t## Dependencies and Gating\n68\t\n69\t- Gated by the TLS migration spike (RHOAIENG-7452): the spike's outcome rewrites this epic's approach. If the spike finds no feasible migration path before the deadline, the team files an OCP exception with a remediation plan and this epic is re-scoped to that plan.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0166ce5350227c5","agent_id":"a9f7d0263db104ceb","session_id":"ffc190d1-a457-4608-ad90-0fad47057ac1","uuid":"fa8f0ecb-d163-4cd9-ba3a-4cb6ebb371af","timestamp":"2026-10-09T14:43:35.749Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfbec7a371a57a13","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
