{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9669300b0174d3b8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E008\n3\ttitle: Remediate trainer data cache TLS stack for ML-KEM hybrid support\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: Training Kubeflow\n6\tteam: Trainer team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8001-E007\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8001-E007\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: remove\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the audit finds an OpenSSL-backed TLS stack, no remediation\n15\t    is needed and this epic is removed (the base image switch delivers PQC); if remediation\n16\t    is required but cannot land by September 15, the trainer team files an OCP exception\n17\t    with a remediation plan.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 0\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: 0\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: Medium\n31\tai_implementability_score: 2\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Remediate trainer data cache TLS stack for ML-KEM hybrid support\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic remediates the trainer data cache's TLS stack to support ML-KEM (FIPS 203) hybrid key exchange — but only if the TLS posture audit (RHOAIENG-7196) determines the component uses a pure-Rust TLS stack that cannot inherit PQC from a base image. If the audit finds an OpenSSL-backed stack, no remediation is needed (the platform-wide base image switch delivers PQC compliance for the component) and this epic is removed.\n40\t\n41\tPer the strategy's Security NFR, Rust components using pure-Rust TLS stacks must support ML-KEM hybrid key exchange after migration. If the remediation cannot land before the September 15, 2026 deadline, the trainer team files an OCP exception via OCPEXCEPT with a remediation plan instead.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Implement the remediation path recommended by the audit so the trainer data cache negotiates ML-KEM hybrid key exchange on its TLS connections.\n46\t- Preserve opportunistic hybrid negotiation — non-PQC TLS 1.3 clients continue to work via classic ECDHE (backwards compatibility NFR).\n47\t- Validate the remediation does not change HA characteristics (no replica or availability changes).\n48\t- If remediation cannot land by September 15: the trainer team files the OCP exception documenting the component's TLS stack and the reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM, with a remediation plan; this epic is then re-scoped to that plan.\n49\t\n50\tOut of scope: the trainer component's base image switch (platform-wide switch campaign); Go ML-KEM and TLS-scanner CI (RHAISTRAT-7816); ML-DSA certificates (deferred).\n51\t\n52\t## Acceptance Criteria\n53\t\n54\t- The data cache negotiates ML-KEM hybrid key exchange after remediation, demonstrated by a test connection against the migrated stack.\n55\t- Non-PQC TLS 1.3 clients continue to connect via classic ECDHE (opportunistic hybrid negotiation preserved).\n56\t- No replica count, availability, or HA characteristic changed as a result of the remediation.\n57\t- Rollback: the TLS stack change is revertible by restoring the prior stack configuration and rebuilding; the fallback path is the OCP exception filing with a documented remediation plan.\n58\t- The remediation (or the exception filing, if that path is taken) is complete before the September 15, 2026 deadline, and the component's tracking ticket is linked to the parent strategy.\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image... for RHOAI 3.6 / OCP 5.0** — delivers this component's route to ML-KEM compliance if the base image switch cannot provide it.\n63\t- **[P0] Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception via OCPEXCEPT with a remediation plan** — the exception path is this epic's recorded fallback.\n64\t- Supports the strategy's Security NFR (ML-KEM hybrid for pure-Rust TLS stacks), Backwards compatibility NFR, and Availability NFR.\n65\t\n66\t## Dependencies and Gating\n67\t\n68\t- Gated by the trainer data cache TLS posture audit (RHOAIENG-7196): if the audit finds an OpenSSL-backed stack, this epic is removed — no remediation is needed. If the audit finds a pure-Rust stack, this epic proceeds on the audit's recommended path.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0166ce5350227c5","agent_id":"a9f7d0263db104ceb","session_id":"ffc190d1-a457-4608-ad90-0fad47057ac1","uuid":"b0291b81-4db8-4ba9-ad53-19f666a5842d","timestamp":"2026-10-09T14:43:43.426Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9669300b0174d3b8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
