{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-916e533263dff0e1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E011\n3\ttitle: TLS handshake latency regression threshold and measurement\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: PerfScale\n6\tteam: Performance team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: -1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: -1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 2\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# TLS handshake latency regression threshold and measurement\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic resolves the strategy's Performance NFR, which is flagged NEEDS DOMAIN INPUT (no numeric regression threshold set; owner: PM + Performance team lead; must be resolved before Sprint 2 ends), and delivers the TLS handshake latency regression measurement required before ship (Performance Team Support: Required).\n34\t\n35\tThe epic defines the numeric TLS handshake latency regression threshold, then measures the RHOAI 3.6 PQC-enabled payload against it, producing the pass/fail evidence for the Availability/Performance NFRs of the base image switch.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Define, with the PM and Performance team lead, the numeric TLS handshake latency regression threshold for the PQC migration — referencing the Chrome ~10% maximum TLS handshake time regression figure and the Red Hat PQC benchmarking outcome (PSASTRAT-7170) cited by the strategy. Resolution is required before Sprint 2 ends.\n40\t- Define the measurement methodology for TLS handshake latency on the PQC-enabled payload (PQC hybrid handshake vs. classic ECDHE baseline), building on the PSASTRAT-7170 benchmarking outcome.\n41\t- Measure TLS handshake latency regression on the RHOAI 3.6 payload once PQC base image switches have landed (PQC-enabled components negotiating ML-KEM hybrid key exchange vs. baseline).\n42\t- Produce a benchmark report: measured regression vs. threshold, per component class where meaningful, with a pass/fail determination.\n43\t- If the measured regression exceeds the threshold: escalate with a remediation plan (the threshold decision determines whether remediation work is required before ship).\n44\t\n45\tOut of scope: remediating performance regressions (follow-on work if the threshold is exceeded); Go ML-KEM benchmarking owned by RHAISTRAT-7816; micro images / Hummingbird-UBI10 base image evolution (post-OCP-5.0).\n46\t\n47\t## Acceptance Criteria\n48\t\n49\t- A numeric TLS handshake latency regression threshold is documented and approved by the PM and Performance team lead before Sprint 2 ends.\n50\t- The measurement methodology is documented, referencing PSASTRAT-7170 and the Chrome ~10% reference.\n51\t- TLS handshake latency is measured on the PQC-enabled RHOAI 3.6 payload against the classic ECDHE baseline, and the measurement completes before ship.\n52\t- The benchmark report records measured regression vs. threshold with a pass/fail determination; any failure is escalated with a remediation plan.\n53\t- The measurement confirms the base image switch has not changed HA characteristics (no availability regression attributable to the switch).\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- Supports the strategy's Performance NFR (⚠️ NEEDS DOMAIN INPUT — this epic resolves it), Availability NFR (no HA changes), and the Prerequisites gate \"Performance Team Support: Required — TLS handshake latency regression measurement needed before ship\".\n58\t- Validates the P0 base image switch HLRs: the switch is only shippable if the measured regression is within the approved threshold.\n59\t\n60\t## Open Questions Addressed\n61\t\n62\t- Resolves the strategy's flagged domain-input gap: no numeric regression threshold set for TLS handshake latency (owner PM + Performance team lead, deadline: before Sprint 2 ends).\n63\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a0166ce5350227c5","agent_id":"a9f7d0263db104ceb","session_id":"ffc190d1-a457-4608-ad90-0fad47057ac1","uuid":"99114fba-6bbc-4d6d-8f8a-8e2f649af7fa","timestamp":"2026-10-09T14:43:55.849Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-916e533263dff0e1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
