 Priority | Epics |\n|-----|----------|-------|\n| All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image (`ubi9-minimal-pqc`, `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`, or equivalent) for RHOAI 3.6 / OCP 5.0 | P0 | E002, E003, E004 (switch delivery); E001 (gating investigation); E006, E008 (non-OpenSSL components' route to ML-KEM compliance); E010 (verification) |\n| Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception via OCPEXCEPT with a remediation plan | P0 | E009 (exception process enforcement, tracking, zero-unaccounted-images accounting); E006, E008 (fallback paths recorded in gate_failure_impact) |\n| PQC enablement is runtime only — only the final stage of the Dockerfile/Containerfile changes; no builder image change needed | P0 | E002, E003, E004 (scope constraint and acceptance criterion on each campaign) |\n| PQC-signed X.509 certificates (ML-DSA) | Deferred | Explicitly out of scope per strategy — no epic, deferred to follow-on phase |\n\nStrategy acceptance criteria allocation: AC-1 (DEFAULT:PQ + ML-KEM kem-algorithms, measured by automated CI scan) → E010 delivers the scan; E002/E003/E004 carry the per-family pass criteria. AC-2 (every image switched or exceptioned by September 15, zero unaccounted) → E009 plus the campaigns. AC-3 (team tracking tickets linked to the parent strategy) → E009.\n\n## Health Warnings (non-blocking)\n\n1. **Performance NFR has no numeric threshold** — flagged NEEDS DOMAIN INPUT, owner PM + Performance team lead, \"must be resolved before Sprint 2 ends\". Modeled as an explicit deliverable and acceptance criterion on E011 rather than a separate Investigation (the threshold value does not change which epics exist; measurement proceeds either way). Requires human follow-up.\n2. **Strategy-level process gates pending human review** — Architecture Review, ODH/RHOAI Build Onboarding, Licence Validation, and Documentation Support are all \"Pending human review\" in Prerequisites & Process Gates. A base image swap is not expected to change transitive dependency licensing (same content, PQC-enabled OpenSSL), but the pending Licence Validation gate is recorded as an unfavorable human-process signal on the campaign epics.\n3. **Documentation Support ambiguity** — listed as \"Pending human review\", not \"Yes\", so no `docs-authoring` epic is included (Rule 11 not triggered). PQC is transparent to users (UXD: Not applicable). If human review confirms documentation support is required, a `docs-authoring` epic should be added at revision.\n4. **NFR vs Technical Approach tension on fms-guardrails-orchestrator** — the Security NFR mandates ML-KEM hybrid support after migration, while the Technical Approach treats an OCP exception as the fallback if the September 15 deadline cannot be met. The decomposition models the migration as gated work (E006) with the exception path recorded as the gate fallback; the exception filing itself is out of scope (each team files its own).\n5. **Priority note** — every epic is P0, matching an all-P0 HLR set under a hard deadline; this is a compliance mandate, not a priority collapse. The only non-P0 strategy item (ML-DSA certificates) is explicitly deferred and excluded.\n6. **TrustyAI explainability service** — expected to file an OCP exception (Java/NSS, not OpenSSL; JDK 29 timeline September 2027). No switch epic is created for it (its base is `ubi9/openjdk-17-runtime`, which has no PQC path; the filing is the team's own out-of-scope work). It is accounted for through E009's readiness matrix and zero-unaccounted-images tracking.\n7. **Scope trap addressed** — AC-1's \"measured by automated CI scan across the RHOAI 3.6 payload\" implies CI infrastructure that does not exist yet; E010 provisions it. FIPS+PQC incompatibility on FIPS-mode clusters is expected behavior for this release and is encoded as an exclusion in E010's acceptance criteria rather than a compliance failure.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nThe AIPCC PQC base image variants (python/nodejs) and the RHEL 9.8 rebase are external dependencies with uncertain timing. Partial value is deliverable without them, so the strategy splits:\n\n- **Tier 1 (independent, start immediately)**: E002 (ubi9-minimal family, ~68 images — confirmed-available target base), E005+E006 (guardrails TLS migration), E007+E008 (trainer data cache), E009 (readiness matrix and coordination), E010 (CI scan), E011 (performance threshold and methodology), E001 itself (risk-reduction confirmation).\n- **Tier 2 (dependency-gated)**: E003 (~34 rhel9-ELS images, gated on the RHEL 9.8 rebase committed date), E004 (~11 python/nodejs images, gated on PQC variant availability).\n\nIf a Tier 2 dependency does not resolve in time, the affected component teams file OCP exceptions by September 15 (tracked by E009); the Tier 1 value — the bulk of the payload on `ubi9-minimal-pqc` — still ships.\n","numLines":117,"startLine":1,"totalLines":117}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-aa637def833093fc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
